# Repo-root build-context excludes. The single source for every image build, all of
# which use the repository root as their context so the resolve layer can read the
# workspace root, the lockfile, and every member's pyproject.
#
# Each Dockerfile then selectively COPYs only the members its image is allowed to
# carry, which is what keeps the api image free of scipy and the learning image free
# of the web stack. This file keeps every context lean and, critically, keeps
# secrets (.env*) and rebuilt artifacts out.

# Rebuilt inside the image (Python toolchain)
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml
**/dist
**/build
**/*.egg-info

# Rebuilt inside the image (JS toolchain)
**/node_modules
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests never ship in an image
**/tests

# VCS, CI, and secrets (.env* keeps any local secret file out of every context)
.git
.gitignore
.github
.env*

# Directories no image build copies
docs
e2e
deployments
# ...except the deployment's own `ops` package, which the ops image carries. It is standard library
# only, so this is the whole of that image's payload.
!deployments/ops

# `frontend` is deliberately NOT excluded: the SPA image the frontend slice adds
# needs it in its context, and the JS toolchain excludes above already keep it lean.

# Root tooling and scratch
docker-compose*.yml
justfile
lefthook.yml
ruff.toml
.secrets.baseline
.DS_Store
